														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1387608">
									

<p>Downvoted for poor voice acting, bad scripting, and even worse planning as to the composition of personnel and nomenclature.</p>
<p>No field personnel talk like that, and they don't speak like such - I dunno, &quot;pansies&quot; I guess is the word - to each other. The concept of a training exercise that designed to hurt, not kill is outright retarded. They're presumably valuable personnel. There's a difference between expendable and disposable. I don't even have words for half of it. A Colonel supervising a Staff Sergeant, a Corporal and several Specialists? Their tasking orders within the &quot;squad&quot; (that's not a squad, by the way)?</p>
<p>Urgh. I think I got diarrhea from reading/listening to this.</p>
<p>I *almost* want to do a TroyL-style blow-by-blow commentary on why this congles mocks, but I couldn't listen to it again.</p>

							</div>

